1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Hello everyone, let's learn about a series of tools to optimize the shape.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
First, let's open the practice file of the fixed needle and the sewing machine.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
In this case, we will use the fixed needle and the sewing machine.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Simulate this scarf and wear it on the model.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
First, to improve the simulation speed, we can freeze or reactivate the following clothes.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
For pieces that have contact with the scarf,

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
which are the collar and front and back pieces,

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
you can choose to freeze it with the right button.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Then you can choose the opposite direction with the right button on the piece that has been selected.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The shortcut key is Ctrl-Shift-I.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Then press the Shift key to select the scarf.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
For other pieces,

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
you can choose to set the anti-aggression plate and sewing line.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
This will further reduce the calculation and speed up the simulation.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
After the preparation is complete, we will deal with the scarf plate.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
In order to prevent the scarf from falling directly when simulated,

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
we need to add a fixed needle to it.

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In the first row of the third tool in the left toolbar,

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
long press to find the fixed needle tool.

20
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Long press to find the fixed needle tool.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
You can see that there is a fixed needle case and a fixed needle set tool at the bottom of the grid tool selection.

22
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
They are just different ways of selection.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Here we choose the fixed needle case tool.

24
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
At this time, the 2D and 3D panels will show a pink grid.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
The method of adding a fixed needle is similar to the method of selecting a grid tool.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Just select the frame on the panel.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
After the frame selection, there will be a red dot at the top of the grid.

28
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
This means that a fixed needle has been added.

29
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,000
At the same time, you can see that the fixed needle selected in the 3D window is orange.

30
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The unselected fixed needle is red.

31
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Now the two sets of fixed needles are selected separately and can be moved separately.

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
So if you want to add a fixed needle multiple times in a set,

33
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
after adding a part of the fixed needle in the frame selection,

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
you can press Ctrl and Shift to add a selection.

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Then the fixed needle selected now is a whole that can be selected and moved together.

36
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Note that the blank area is not possible to cancel the fixed needle selection.

37
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
This is different from selecting a grid tool.

38
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
If you want to delete the fixed needle, you can select it by pressing Ctrl at the 2D window.

39
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Or on the 3D panel, right-click on the fixed needle and select Delete.

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
There is a little trick here.

41
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
We can add a fixed needle on the line where we need to add a fixed needle.

42
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Just double-click, you can quickly create a row of fixed needles along the line.

43
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,000
We add two rows of fixed needles on the edges of the scarf.

44
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Then in the middle of the scarf, the position of the model in front of you.

45
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Add two rows of fixed needles.

46
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
You can refer to the position in the video.

47
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
If you accidentally misselect the scarf grid at the back,

48
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:35,000
you can press Ctrl and select the fixed needle that does not need to be selected.

49
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
After adding the fixed needle,

50
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,000
switch the tool to the move tool and turn on the simulation.

51
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Now the goal is to put the two ends of the scarf into the ring on the outside of it.

52
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
We can first press the Shift key in the 3D window.

53
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Click on the two rows of fixed needles in front of the model.

54
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Then adjust the position of the ball.

55
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Turn to the side view.

56
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Move them a little bit to the front of the model.

57
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Leave a space for operation.

58
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Pay attention here.

59
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
When you move the fixed needle, if you stop the simulation,

60
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:16,000
then only the part of the grid selected by the fixed needle will move with it.

61
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
If you move the fixed needle in the simulation state,

62
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
then the selected grid will take other grids on the board.

63
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Then select the fixed needle on the right edge.

64
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Draw the position of the ball.

65
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Press the shortcut key 2 to the front of the model.

66
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Use the position of the ball to move the fixed needle up and move it to the left.

67
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Place it in the top position of the scarf that can pass through the scarf.

68
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Make a trend from top to bottom.

69
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Then right-click to rotate the view.

70
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
You can press the Shift key to rotate the view.

71
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Then press the Shift key to rotate the view.

72
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Press the Shift key to rotate the view.

73
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Then press the Shift key to rotate the view.

74
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:58,000
You can feel the obvious stop at the 90-degree rotation angle.

75
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Turn to the side.

76
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
If you find that the fixed needle is a little bit too thick,

77
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:06,000
then we can use the positioning ball to move it forward a little bit

78
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
so that it can pass through the scarf smoothly.

79
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
This way, we can ensure that

80
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
whether it is on the front or on the side,

81
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
the fixed needle is in the inner top of the circle of the scarf,

82
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:24,000
and then use the positioning ball to move the whole thing downward to pass through the scarf.

83
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Be careful not to pull it too tight.

84
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
The left side is also operated in the same way.

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Because the left side itself is on the inside,

86
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
it needs to be rotated from the bottom to the outside,

87
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
and then to the circle and to the inside once.

88
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
The same can be combined with the view.

89
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Move the fixed needle to the inside of the scarf in the front,

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
where it can pass through,

91
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:54,000
and make sure that the side is also in the angle and position where it can pass through smoothly.

92
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
After the fixed needle passes through this side,

93
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:02,000
it needs to be turned to the front and rotated to the outside.

94
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Repeat the process of going inside again.

95
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Here is a small suggestion.

96
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,000
When using the fixed needle adjustment,

97
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
it is recommended that you pause frequently.

98
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Then turn on the simulation pause.

99
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
You can record the current form,

100
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:28,000
and avoid going back to the initial simulation state when canceling.

101
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
After both sides are worn,

102
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
the scarf is now loose.

103
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,000
We can bring the fixed needle reserved in the front closer to the model

104
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
to tighten the scarf.

105
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:44,000
You can press the Shift key to select the fixed needle on both ends of the scarf.

106
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Use the positioning ball to move down together.

107
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
After adjusting to the satisfied position,

108
00:06:51,000 --> 00:07:01,000
right-click to delete this part of the fixed needle,

109
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:09,000
or press the Ctrl and W keys to delete all fixed needles.

110
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
In order to make the simulation effect of the scarf more natural and real,

111
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,000
we can reduce the particle diameter of the scarf to 10 mm,

112
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
and change the thickness of the scarf to 1 mm,

113
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:33,000
and then simulate again.

114
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
In addition to the way of adding a fixed needle in the frame selection,

115
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:41,000
we can also add a single-point fixed needle in 3D.

116
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
While pressing the W key,

117
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:47,000
we want to add the position of the fixed needle on the 3D costume.

118
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Right-click on it,

119
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
and add a single-point fixed needle.

120
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
The position of the fixed needle can also be moved,

121
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
and we can start the simulation.

122
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Drag the point of the fixed needle directly to adjust the overall shape.

123
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
If you want to delete the fixed needle,

124
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
right-click to delete,

125
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
or press the W key,

126
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:20,000
right-click again to delete the fixed needle.

127
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Next, I will introduce the sewing tool.

128
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
You can use the sewing tool to adjust the shape of the scarf.

129
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Select the sewing tool.

130
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Click on two points on the board.

131
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:38,000
You can use either 3D or 2D.

132
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
These two selected points

133
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,000
will be connected by a blue curve.

134
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:49,000
You can switch to the edit sewing tool to check.

135
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
You can use the edit sewing tool

136
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
to move these two points again.

137
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
After opening the simulation,

138
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:05,000
these two points will be connected and fixed together.

139
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
We can use this tool,

140
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,000
to adjust the shape of the scarf,

141
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
for example,

142
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
adjust the shape of the scarf on the right side.

143
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
For adding a good sewing,

144
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
you can adjust the position of the two ends of the line,

145
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:29,000
and then turn on the simulation to adjust the shape.

146
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:34,000
The sewing tool can also be used to pull the distance of the scarf on both sides.

147
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
You can adjust the length of the line.

148
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
You can adjust the length of the line.

149
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
You can adjust the length of the line.

150
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
You can also adjust the length of the line.

151
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
You can adjust the length of the line.

152
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
The default distance of the two points of the sewing is 0 mm.

153
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Select the curve connected by this line.

154
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
In the right-hand attribute editor,

155
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
change the length of the line to the appropriate value,

156
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
such as 30 to 50 mm.

157
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
According to the effect adjustment,

158
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:31,000
you can add 1 to 2 sets of this type of push.

159
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
You can further reduce the diameter of the scarf to 5 mm,

160
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:42,000
and turn on the simulation.

161
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Finally, double-click to select all the sweater sheets.

162
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Press the Shift key and select all the skirt sheets.

163
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,000
Right-click to select Activate.

164
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Then press the Control key to simulate again,

165
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
making the scarf and clothes fit more naturally.

166
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
The completed file can be saved by itself.

167
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Next, I will introduce the range drag tool.

168
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Open the practice file.

169
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Usually, when we simulate dragging clothes,

170
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
we use the point drag.

171
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Sometimes, it can also be switched to the range drag according to the need.

172
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
For example, this one has a twisted strap.

173
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Now the left-hand panel

174
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
is connected to the bottom of the right-hand panel.

175
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
We need to pull it out

176
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:32,000
to form an intersectional twist.

177
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
One idea is to use the selection grid tool.

178
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Pull out the grid that is connected to the bottom.

179
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
There is also a more convenient way,

180
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
which is to use the range drag.

181
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
First, turn on the simulation.

182
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Move the grid of the fixed needle on the left side of the screen out.

183
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Now we only need to move the grid of the lower part of the left panel to the outside.

184
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
In the simulation,

185
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
select the move tool as a small grab.

186
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Long press the icon to switch to the range drag.

187
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,000
At this time, the mouse will become two same-center circles.

188
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
The inner circle is the core selection area.

189
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
The outer circle is the reduction range.

190
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
In the set panel that is displayed on the right side,

191
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
we can first select the display weight.

192
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
It is convenient for us to check the selected area.

193
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
In the 3D window,

194
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
left-click to drag.

195
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:41,000
You can move the entire area of the selected green highlight.

196
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Because this area is smaller,

197
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:50,000
we make the range of the soft selection smaller.

198
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:55,000
The degree of reduction determines the degree of drag force.

199
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
In the surface mode,

200
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
the drag effect is only applied to the specified range.

201
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
The surface of each selected layer,

202
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
the drag effect is only applied to the specified range.

203
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
In the straight line mode,

204
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,000
you can choose all panels within a certain range of 10 points.

205
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Whether the selected panel and the other layers of the panel are together,

206
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:19,000
the measurement method is to change back to the surface.

207
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Turn to the side view,

208
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
left-click to press the mouse to move outward,

209
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:29,000
you can easily move the lower part of the panel out.

210
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
After dragging out,

211
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
remove the fixed pin and simulate again.

212
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:38,000
The twist is done.

213
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Press and hold again to select the moving tool.

214
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:53,000
You can switch back to the way of clicking and dragging.

215
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Finally, let's look at the difference between hardening and shape solidification.

216
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Open the practice file,

217
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
here are two T-shirts on the ground.

218
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Now the shape is the same.

219
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:13,000
You can switch to only display the 3D window.

220
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
We are on this dress on the left side.

221
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
After double-clicking,

222
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
right-click to select hardening,

223
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
press the shortcut key,

224
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Ctrl plus H.

225
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,000
At this time,

226
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
this dress will turn orange.

227
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
After opening the simulation,

228
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
you can see that the original wrinkles are gone.

229
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
All wrinkles have been opened.

230
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Its material will temporarily become like rubber,

231
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
very hard.

232
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Hardening is often used to flatten the fabric

233
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:44,000
or deal with severe curls.

234
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Right-click again to choose to remove hardening.

235
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
It will restore the original soft attribute.

236
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Now look at the dress on the right side.

237
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Double-click to select this T-shirt,

238
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:02,000
and then right-click to select shape solidification.

239
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Press the shortcut key,

240
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Ctrl plus E.

241
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
After opening the simulation,

242
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:10,000
you will find that its wrinkle form has not changed at all.

243
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
When we drag it in the simulation state,

244
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
it is moving as a whole.

245
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:20,000
The original wrinkles and shape are firmly fixed,

246
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
and it is not easy to change.

247
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
You can drag the T-shirt on the left side without solidification to compare.

248
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
The solidified clothes are still physically simulated

249
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
and can also be moved,

250
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
but it always maintains the shape of the solidification at that moment.

251
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Solidification and shape solidification

252
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
are used to adjust the needs of various clothing styles.

253
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
